# Agent runtime (platform)

Full map: **`docs/AGENT_RUNTIME.md`**.

## Non-negotiables

- Claude = **Agent SDK `query()`** via `askClaude` → `ClaudeRuntime` (`lib/claude-runtime.ts`). Default `CLAUDE_RUNTIME=sdk` (bundled Claude Code CLI + OAuth; coding tools disabled). `cli` = hotfix `claude -p`. Not Anthropic Messages API. Vision on SDK path uses explicit `cli_vision_fallback` (logged).
- Customer tools = in-process MCP `mcp__platform__*` + `canUseTool` (host still executes book/collect in `conversation.ts`). CLI hotfix keeps the text `<tool_call>` protocol.
- Within a turn: **one session** — tenant reply model keeps a single `--resume` id (`lib/turn-claude-sessions.ts`). Tool follow-ups continue that session (no Haiku hop). Mid-turn prompt activate clears the resume id and aborts in-flight Claude (`AbortSignal`).
- Process hygiene: CLI spawn is a detached process group; abort/timeout kills the group and logs if pid is alive after 2s. `CLAUDE_WARMUP_ON_START` → `runtime.warmup()` (does not arm quota circuit, does not take IG/meta semaphore). Health-check warns on orphan `claude` (ppid 1) without failing.
- Tenant reply model = **sonnet \| opus** only (`normalizeClaudeReplyModel`). The same model handles first spawn and tool follow-ups. Haiku is warmup / usage probe only.
- CRM only via `getCrmAdapter` + `resolveCrmProvider(action)` — never HTTP in `conversation.ts`.
- Platform capability map lives in `lib/platform-capabilities-prompt.ts` — inject into **meta-agent** and **insights (AI-помічник)**. Keep in sync when changing modes/tools/CRM.
- Spawn CWD is isolated (`claude-spawn-cwd`) — tenant disk `CLAUDE.md` is **not** the customer system prompt; DB `system_prompts` + runtime injections are.
- Telegram manager alerts are **side effects**, not a customer-facing tool.

